n interesting  character arc as luffy struggles to  regain control of his body and his  powers and honestly it would kind of  make sense for something like this to  happen from everything we know so far  luffy's new powers are absolutely  incredible and if there is not some sort  of serious drawback to using them they  will be absolutely broken i mean luffy  could theoretically just breeze through  the rest of the story on easy mode and  absolutely wreck every obstacle that  stands in his way with his new godly  power but if using this power comes at  the price of temporarily being possessed  by another entity and or losing control  of yourself and going berserk then luffy  will have to struggle long and hard in  order to fully master his new power and  that means that he won't be able to just  speedrun elbaf and laughtale he still  has a long way to go and the villains  including blackbeard the admirals and  emu still have a chance of defeating him  i mean as much as any villain has a  chance of defeating a shonen protagonist  so i predict that using his new godly  powers will come at a great cost to  luffy this cost may come in the form of  losing control and going berserk or  maybe even being outright possessed by  joyboy whose will or essence has been  residing within the devil fruit formerly  known as the gomu gomu nomi so luffy  will need to work harder than ever  before to master this new power without  losing control and he will have to come  to terms with an alien will living  inside of him the will of joy boy and  speaking of wills i feel like a lot of  people talk about inherited will in one  piece but they never bother actually  explaining what this means often when  they talk about it it feels like they're  just talking about an idea like the idea  of freedom so it's like joy boy believed  in freedom and now luffy believes in  freedom so when they say that luffy  inherited joy boy's will it's almost  like he inherited his ideology but  clearly there is 